{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage","id":926567,"title":"[2e] Why Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-05T12:39:50-07:00","id":926567,"title":"[2e] Why Mage?","content":"I couldn't see one of these for Mage, so I thought I'd start it. Can you sell Mage to me? I own 1st ed and I have the advance preview of 2nd. I've loved the three games released so far in the 2nd edition rules (Vampire, Werewolf, and Demon) and I was looking forward to Mage. However, something about it is just not clicking in my head. The magic system is great, that's without question. But I just can't seem to break in to this one.<br /> <br /> How would you encourage someone to pick it up over the other CofD games and run it instead?<br /> What amazing things have you done or seen so far?<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing what you have to say.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:15:05-07:00","id":926589,"title":"","content":"While I can't speak on 2e directly as I haven't ran it yet (and not sure if I will. There are things I like and things I hate about it.), Mage in general is a game that is heavily a shared experience. The ST can't describe to you how magic looks as it is different for each mage. The players have to add their own flare to such descriptions. This aspect is what I like about mage. It can be as ugly or pretty as the player is able to speak about their magic. This can make for a really beautifully game if you have people who can describe things well.<br /> <br /> The personal horror nature of the game (the fact that most mages can't really still be around Sleeper friends and family, or at the very least having this secret life that none of them know about) is something that when is played on, and done well, is something that can be rather scary. Stories about how a mage tries to maintain relationships with Sleepers while trying not to invoke paradox (and thus the attention of the Guardians of the Veil) could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Mage, to me, asks two questions mainly: 1) 'should I do this?' (rather than 'can', because chances are you mostly likely can do it) and 2) 'What happens when you give x person the power of god?'<br /> The first is more for character development and perhaps is a minor point, but the second? Scary things can happen if you include this question as a plot point(ex: 'What happens if Hitler was a mage?')<br /> <br /> In all, Mage provides the most choices for stories, how to do things, I think. In some ways, too many choice and that trying to figure out just what you want to do in a game can be the hardest part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:25:11-07:00","id":926637,"title":"","content":"Mage: if you have to go mad, at least you can go mad with power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:43:46-07:00","id":926651,"title":"","content":"Mage enables you to get involved with a wide range of mysteries and weirdness. To explore stories about what separates you from others, and how you would apply your power. It is great for telling stories of slow spirals into obsession and madness, where your PCs can start with the best of intentions, and look back at the Chronicle's end to see how they became it's villains through small choices.<br /> <br /> Leverage the damage you can inflict upon others unwillingly or unwittingly with Paradox, Dissonance, and Nimbus.<br /> Add in some Lovecraftian Horror with Paradox, Abyssals, and Lower Depths.<br /> Play out classical Mystery stories that only a Mage could solve through their talents - and show them what happens when they grow too cocky and leap to conclusions.<br /> Add some sense of Cold War, opposition, and oppression with the Seers of the Throne.<br /> Throw players broken mirrors and curve-balls with the Mad.<br /> Run a spiritual trial or vision quest with Supernal Entities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T15:42:15-07:00","id":926688,"title":"","content":"Mage is a game about mystery more than any other line in CofD. So, for people that love multiple ongoing mysteries, that's great. <br /> <br /> Having played...about four sessions so far in a 2e game, I have to say that it's been a blast. We have a hilarious player that has an Acanthus character and he really plays up the whole fool archetype. Also, none of us are very much into horror, so the ST plays down that aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, if it isn't clicking for you AND you've played a session, then it just might not be the game for you. If you haven't played a session, I'd give it a try just to see if there's an aspect you might like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:35:39-07:00","id":926708,"title":"","content":"If you believe - or at least consider it to be possible - that only thing stopping people from being terrible, horrible beings is lack of opportunity and fear of being caught and punished, Mage is the horroriest horror of the horrors, because it's about people who have been cursed with opportunity and with immunity to being caught or judged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:46:36-07:00","id":926713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=926708#post926708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's about people who have been cursed with opportunity and with immunity to being caught or judged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially True. It drastically reduces the pool of people/beings with the resources and ability to catch you or judge your crimes to a very finite number. Also it turns you into one of those few people capable of catching and judging people like yourself, and asks the question: Are you willing to put your neck on the line as one of the only people able to solve certain types of injustice?<br /> <br /> A very &quot;Supervillian vs Super Hero/Antihero&quot; scaling of morality in terms of power.<br /> <br /> But I love the Lovecraft themes, and Mysteries beyond sane comprehension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-05-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:13:50-07:00","id":926749,"title":"","content":"Sure, vampires can hypnotize you into being a walking blood bag and make you enjoy it. Werewolves can tear you limb from limb. Prometheans poison the environment and warp your mind by simply existing. Changelings feed on your emotions. Demons steal bits of your identity that you sell to them. <br /> <br /> But anything any other splat can do, mages can do. Maybe even better. They walk around, routinely rewriting the laws of reality to suit their purposes, and the universe sometimes doesn't even fight back. What else can you call a being who can cast a spell that makes it so that you suffered a third-degree burn <i>a week ago</i>, can conjure gamma radiation <i>ex nihil</i>, can return the dead to life... but a god? Yes, in many ways, a mage is a god. The best ones realize that it's probably not courteous to carve your name in North America so big that it's visible from orbit. The worst ones practically see it as their birthright to do that. <br /> <br /> Yet at the same time, Mage 2e has a strangely hopeful tone. It's remarkably egalitarian: anyone, regardless of race, creed, nationality, class, sex, or sexual preference can become a mage. The bad guys want to create a system of haves and have-nots because they have delicate egos. A wrong has been written, and best-case scenario, you are taking a big, magical eraser and righting that wrong one person at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:54:06-07:00","id":926770,"title":"","content":"Wait, are you asking to be sold on Mage in general, or are you asking to be sold on making the switch to Mage 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:09:38-07:00","id":926776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=926770#post926770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are you asking to be sold on Mage in general, or are you asking to be sold on making the switch to Mage 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good clarifying question. The Original poster did mention they already had 1e. I hadn't given that too much weight but your question does bring into focus that the other posters and I may have been misunderstanding the Original Poster's intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T20:06:56-07:00","id":926797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solarious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=926637#post926637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: if you have to go mad, at least you can go mad with power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You ever tried going mad without power? It's boring. No one listens to you!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Anyone who gets the reference, I love you.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T20:13:00-07:00","id":926801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=926776#post926776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good clarifying question. The Original poster did mention they already had 1e. I hadn't given that too much weight but your question does bring into focus that the other posters and I may have been misunderstanding the Original Poster's intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, the OP also already bought 2e. I confess I do not actually understand what the request is either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T01:46:27-07:00","id":926928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=926797#post926797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You ever tried going mad without power? It's boring. No one listens to you!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Anyone who gets the reference, I love you.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I got it, was thinking the same thing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2476\" data-vbnamecard=\"2476\">Aethers</a> What do you mean it's not clicking? Like, you've already stated you like the mechanics, so is it the fluff? Because the fluff didn't change significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-06-2016, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T03:18:36-07:00","id":945383,"title":"","content":"Hi, sorry for not replying sooner (and sorry for rezzing a dead thread). Life stuff got in the way. If you've never planned a wedding before, it can eat your life...<br /> <br /> To answer <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and @Mrmduois: I guess it's the core setting of Mage that has never really clicked. I've played Mage: Ascension once, and Mage: the Awakening 1st ed in one or two one-offs, but it's not grabbed me. I don't know what the story should be. Compared to the others, you can &quot;get&quot; them pretty quickly. You can explain the core of Vampire, Werewolf, Demon, Hunter, etc in a sentence.<br /> <br /> This is in part to the fact that I hate using PDFs. I spend all day on a computer, I don't want to have to spend my reading time using one too. I will get a POD version of Mage when it comes out and I know this will make a different on how much I take in. I haven't read more than the five splats section, and a quick bit of character gen so far.<br /> <br /> From what you have said, and from your experiences, could you run Mage similar to X-Files or Fringe? Ie, something horrific and unexplained happens, then the players have to investigate and find out how and why this happened? Would that be a good place to start a campaign?<br /> <br /> Thank you<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T03:37:20-07:00","id":945387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aethers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=945383#post945383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Compared to the others, you can &amp;quot;get&amp;quot; them pretty quickly. You can explain the core of Vampire, Werewolf, Demon, Hunter, etc in a sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ungodly, almost unlimited power wrapped up in an arrogant prick being called human race. Good luck. &quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T03:54:24-07:00","id":945392,"title":"","content":"I think one of the main concepts about mage is that it is.. magical!! And the fact is that mage is a really messy and big giant concept to envelop in one book. U can literally play anything any genre story or plot u want to set up for your players. <br /> <br /> Do u want a bloody plotting game of thrones style that will make even elder vampires tremble in fear? Try to cook something up with mastigos and acanthus manipulating minD souls and time to achieve their objectives. An acanthus can set up plans to overgrown entire cabasl and cities when the fate wheel starts spinning and mastigos can eradicate minds creating puppets like elder vampires.<br /> <br /> Do u want extreme shootouts bloody gore and violence on the street with cabals killing each other on sight? U can do that. Cabals will probably start wars over artifacts books or spell rotes now. <br /> <br /> Do u want a Terrifying spy game where u canT trust nobody and u become a paranoid member of a creepy sect that is ready to kill and hide even the most infamous secrets from human and awakened society? Join the guardians.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do want an all out war and special forces operation feeling ? Join the adamantine arrow. A veteran arrow cabal can easily hunt down a pack of werewolves or eradicate a coterie if they need to. <br /> <br /> Do u simply want to wander around in wonder exploring magic mistery and wonders and try to solve enigma puzzles or riddles set up by gods spirits and weird creatures? Explore the dream world and spirit world, ghosts hexes.. hidden curses and occult societies ? I think the misterium and the entire mage society is for u.<br /> <br /> <br /> U can play mage like a true detective story, a doctor who epic saga or a game of thrones gritty and backstabbing plot.<br /> <br /> Or u c\u00e1n throw everything out of the window and play an Indiana Jones style chronicle where ur players crawl in jungles and Tibetan monasteris looking for Atlantidean artifacts and the location of the watchtowers. <br /> <br /> Is that enough? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:16:07-07:00","id":945421,"title":"","content":"Similarly unsure as to OP's exact question too, but I can offer some insight as to why I started running 2e. Its mix of the Matrix and Hogwarts is stylish enough in itself, but really, Mage is about the horror of knowledge. Acquiring knowledge means you can do *anything*, but it comes with it fears unto itself. Knowledge that there are monsters constantly trying to get in, that reality is malleable and broken, that everyone is watched all the time by uncaring gods, that ordinary people are regularly abused but never have any idea about it. That knowledge confers extraordinary power, but it comes with it a complete disintegration of the world as you know it. Consider, as one simple example, the Mastigos. Progressing in their Ruling Arcana means becoming increasingly aware that our minds are playthings of magic, and that objective distance is a fable. What exactly does that *do* to one's sense of self is a fascinating question in its own right. What even is a &quot;person&quot;, to one that now knows thoughts and memories and being in a discrete position are all rubbish lies they can twist at will? Brief glimmer of my feeling but there you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:25:12-07:00","id":945429,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2476\" data-vbnamecard=\"2476\">Aethers</a> running Mage like X-Files? That's pretty much what the game is all about. The politics and other stuff is cool, but there are quite a few people who come on the forums with plans to ditch it all and just play the bit about solving Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:35:18-07:00","id":945436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2476\" data-vbnamecard=\"2476\">Aethers</a> For Awakening, Fringe and X-files are basically a mission statement. However, Mages will solve any Mystery you throw at them - it's what they do. The real fun begins when they have to decide what to do about it. Every slip-up on their part can lead to someone being thrown under the bus, and since Mages have all the power, they have all the responsibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:44:08-07:00","id":945440,"title":"","content":"Mage is like... Doctor Who! Yeah, I see you your eyes rolls, but stay with me...<br /> <br /> Each Doctor Who episode starts with Mystery he and his companions must solve. But it's only half of equation - Doctor surely will understand his and crack open, you know this just because you know the series. Then comes 'magical' moment when Doctor needs to decide to what to <i>do</i> with situation. And then you are understanding why Time Lords are described as near-gods in universe. See this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w4xm9NHNUf8\" data-code=\"w4xm9NHNUf8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/w4xm9NHNUf8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And then you understand why mages are mental monsters... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:18:28-07:00","id":945587,"title":"","content":"Copying a thing I wrote elsewhere:<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;M:tAw is about the moment when the veil is torn back, when you <i>understand</i> the higher Truths of the universe in a thunderbolt of insight, and you realize that this understanding, this <i>gnosis</i> means you can do things you couldn't before. This understanding is singularly addictive: once you've tasted that power, you're compelled to seek out more of it, searching for things that do not make sense and tearing away at them until you unlock their secrets and feel the rush of power that comes from a broader and deeper understanding in those universal Truths. But of course, it isn't all sunshine and rainbows on the road to godhood: for some reason, something is holding you back, and it has always held you back. There's an intelligence that tells you that you shouldn't want to know, called Exarch, and there's a maliciousness that punishes you when you reach too far, called Paradox. But despite these things, you <i>are</i> on the Path to godhood, and damn the consequences that happen along the way.&quot;</div> </span></span><br /> <br /> The core of Mage 2e is in three mechanics: Gnosis, Obsession, and Wisdom. After that, you need to understand the Reach and Paradox mechanics.<br /> <br /> In terms of setting, you need to know what the Lie is, but other than that... &quot;Weird shit is everywhere. Messing around with it has consequences.&quot;<br /> <br /> Everything else is detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:34:47-07:00","id":945713,"title":"","content":"What I really like about Mage in comparison to the other major splats is that your character is human, without being a helpless human, and you can play them however you want. They can be as depraved as the most blood encrusted elder, has violent as a Rahu on roids, or you can play them as a straight up paladin and saint, they can be super sleuths, superspies or Chuck Norris. The sin of pride leaves far more room for variation than rage or blood lust. You can also play whatever flavor of chronicle you like, they aren't tied down by territory, dietary needs or the lethal rays of the sun, but they can also claim a territory and fight for power in Machiavellian courts. You can play Cthullu, DnD or the Bourne Identity, whatever you feel like without having to rewrite fundamental parts of the setting. YOU CAN EVEN PLAY THE HERO!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:47:41-07:00","id":945800,"title":"","content":"My favorite part about mage is the mystery and investigation. And Mage 2e has taken mage1e, already a pretty cool interesting game, cut a lot of the chaff and added more flexibility. And my favorite part is that to become stronger/ more knowledgeable you have to delve into those investigations and odd mysteries. The mechanics facilitate that kind of play. And definitely a lot of posters have hit upon the other key themes that are really well done.<br /> <br /> I would hazard to say that the themes of the Lie aren't even the important part, but merely the lens mages choices to see the world through. For those on one side, it's fake and malleable, but for those on the other side, IT Very F*(king Real and Concrete.<br /> <br /> Week Long Edit: And actually this is still true for some mages. I'm thinking about the different paths. They all have an inferior arcane, a part of the world still locked to them. All the paths see very clear around one corner of the meta narrative. (I wouldn't use the term 'The Lie' as it is a misnowmer to me anyways) But at the same time they are blinded to their obtuse corner. Something I was just thinking about","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 08-09-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:59:52-07:00","id":946898,"title":"","content":"Mage is a game about secret truths, obsession and the corrupting effects of wielding god-like power.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, you dived into the rabbit hole and came out different. You are Awakened now, and see the mundane world for what it is. A fabrication, an illusion. A Lie. The world you once thought you knew is like a cardboard cutout of people and places now, and the weird and supernatural drip and leak at the edges of perception. There is no escape from the nagging sensations the occult world feeds you. And if you look, if you really LOOK, the world unravels before your eyes and the truths of Reality might burn your retina, etching visions of power into your brain.<br /> <br /> The Awakening does not just grant a passive understanding of the world, though. For every time you push at the edges of perception, reality bends and twists according to your will. Suddenly, you no longer need to wait for a taxi, you align the threads of causality to bring one to your doorstep. You don't need to wait for the police to catch a criminal, you know where he's hiding and see the spirits around his bolt hole, waiting for the right words to feast on him. You don't need to wait and resign yourself and grieve for the inevitable death: you can do something about it, and the price to pay for it is not out of reach. When the time comes for you to make a decision about all of these, will you choose what is Wise? Will you choose what is right? Will you be able to live with yourself knowing what you had to do to make it to the end?<br /> <br /> That's the sort of game Mage is. Choose wisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:18:55-07:00","id":947220,"title":"","content":"Thank you to everyone that commented. I have a much clearer idea of how to create the story-basis, and how to sell it to the players. &quot;Phenominal cosmic powers, ity bity living space&quot;<br /> <br /> A special thank you to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> . The Dr Who / Mage description is fantastic, and most likely the kind of thing I would roll with. Set the players as a group of investigators, then do a weekly mystery. Eventually building to a finale that they have had a huge part in creating.<br /> <br /> Now to find the time to finish the book, then round up some players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:02:37-07:00","id":947399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aethers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926567-2e-why-mage?p=947220#post947220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A special thank you to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> . The Dr Who / Mage description is fantastic, and most likely the kind of thing I would roll with. Set the players as a group of investigators, then do a weekly mystery. Eventually building to a finale that they have had a huge part in creating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important part is that after solving Mystery, should come part where PCs decide what to <b><i>do</i></b> with that thing they uncover, 'Oh, we will negotiate Secorax and make them leave the planet' is possible solution ( for high Wisdom Awakened ). But most mages are more likely 'I will burn his home and trap him in every mirror in reality'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You can also make it less 'each weekly episode' but more like Doctor's season - each Mystery is chained to the one great Mystery of chronicle. Like I run Alchemy based game now, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/825300-cod-mage-magnum-opus-actual-play\">Magnum Opus</a></b> - main Mystery is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone\">Philosophers Stone</a>, but by it's nature it's connected to both <i>Uncrowned Kings</i> Legacy and Prometheans as race and phenomenon. Both things can show up in story, adding next layer for both 'mysterieness' and knowledge players can use to exploit - 'You say Promethens can create for us this super duper magical Stones? Let's get one for ourselves! (,,,) Wait, it can kill him? So maybe we should think about it? Naahh, let's get ourselves a Created!'<br /> <br /> Crux of <b>Mage</b> is uncovering knowledge <i>and using it </i>in play! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-09-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:34:35-07:00","id":947426,"title":"","content":"And, well, of course you can look over main inspirations for game - <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Hellblazer_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Hellblazer</a> frenchise ( with good <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5mQ5nqyw3M\" target=\"_blank\">Constantine TV series</a> ) and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dresden_Files\" target=\"_blank\">Dresden Files</a> books ( TV series can be a bit cheesy, but I still like it ). There is also a large <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations\">Inspiration topic</a> on this very forum, started by official compilation from main gameline developer, <b>Dave Brookshaw</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:28:08-07:00","id":948848,"title":"","content":"A Mage could, in theory, sit quietly around for the rest of their life, never using their magic and not really being any different from any other human. That might seem like a strange selling point, but for me it's the key difference between playing Mage and anything else in the Chronicles of Darkness. The reason a Mage goes on adventures is because they choose to go out there and interact with the world. Their motivation isn't some alien hunger for blood like vampires or strange spiritual nature like werewolves. Their motivations are either curiosity for the noble mages or a lust for power for the more selfish. Either way those are very easy motivations to connect with as a player and they tend to give you very active and self-directed characters.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller you don't need to craft complex political justifications about how the group can work together or try to manipulate everyone into going on the quest. All you need to do with a group of Mages is give them a mystery. If you say &quot;By the way, there's a rumour that there's a small town out in the countryside where every single flower growing turns black under the light of the full moon&quot; the players will usually answer &quot;When's the next flight out there and can I get a ticket?&quot;<br /> <br /> One of my Mage games I ran one week without any particular plot in mind so the players loaded up the wikipedia page of a nearby town and looked up the interesting and mysterious places there which they decided to proactively investigate and see if any of them had a capital M mystery involved.<br /> <br /> Just be aware that Mages are very very good at solving mysteries. A single spell could unravel the plot of most detective novels straight away, sometimes they don't even need a spell when just Magesight on its own gives you a lot of information. Designing mysteries for Mages is a bit different from designing a mystery for anyone else and it can take a bit of practice to get the hang of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":".  whoops, typo. 08-11-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}